      <div class="port"><i></i>APT mirror</div>
    </div>
    <div class="patch-foot">Magenta for plumbing, red for keeping watch, blue for apps</div>
  </div>
  <div class="entries">
    <article class="entry rv" style="--k:4">
      <h3>DEB Party</h3>
      <p>Turns a short list of GitHub projects into a tidy .deb mini-mirror. Picks the right release asset, repackages bare binaries, prunes old versions and publishes through Aptly. The gauges ship through it.</p>
      <div class="meta">Python, Aptly</div>
      <div class="links"><a href="https://deb.arzaroth.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">deb.arzaroth.com</a><a href="https://github.com/Arzaroth/deb.arzaroth.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a></div>
    </article>
    <article class="entry rv" style="--k:5">
      <h3>Code lives at home too</h3>
      <p>Every repository here lives on a Forgejo instance on the rack. Server-side mirrors push it to GitHub, which is only the shop window.</p>
      <div class="meta">Forgejo, Forgejo Actions</div>
      <div class="links"><a href="https://git.arzaroth.com/Arzaroth" target="_blank" rel="noopener">git.arzaroth.com</a></div>
    </article>
    <article class="entry rv" style="--k:6">
      <h3>dotfiles</h3>
      <p>Zsh, Emacs, tmux and prompt configuration as GNU Stow packages. Arch on the desk, Debian on the servers.</p>
      <div class="meta">Emacs Lisp, shell</div>
      <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/Arzaroth/dotfiles" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a></div>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CONTRIBUTIONS -->
<section class="pane" id="contributions" style="--c:var(--c-orange)">
  <div class="pane-head">
    <div class="slot rv" style="--k:0">U17-18</div>
    <h2 class="rv" style="--k:1">Other people's code</h2>
    <p class="lede rv" style="--k:2">A friend's desktop toys I contribute to, and patches sent upstream, mostly because a job needed them.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="friends">
    <article class="entry rv" style="--k:3">
      <div class="count"><span data-count="23">23</span><small>pull requests</small></div>
      <h3>doot</h3>
      <p>A trumpet-playing skeleton that pops up at random on your screen from September 1st to October 31st. Among my contributions: native Wayland overlays, native audio output, encrypted achievement sync between machines, and the move to uv.</p>
      <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/boubou666/doot/pulls?q=is%3Apr+author%3AArzaroth" target="_blank" rel="noopener">My pull requests</a></div>
    </article>
    <article class="entry rv" style="--k:4">
      <div class="count"><span data-count="4">4</span><small>pull requests</small></div>
      <h3>butbutbut</h3>
      <p>A goal goes in, in Ligue 1, the Premier League, LaLiga, Serie A, the Bundesliga or a European cup, and the horn plays with the score on your screen. Among my contributions: native audio, a daemon that follows the session, and auto-update.</p>
      <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/boubou666/butbutbut/pulls?q=is%3Apr+author%3AArzaroth" target="_blank" rel="noopener">My pull requests</a></div>
    </article>
  </div>
  <div class="upstream-wrap rv" style="--k:5">
    <table class="upstream">
      <caption>Landed upstream</caption>
